description:
Design a n-bit Johnson counter that generates a specific sequence of binary states based on the current state of a series of flip-flops. When the clock signal (clk) rises, the counter shifts its state, inverting the last flip-flop's output and shifting it into the lowest bit position, effectively creating a circular pattern. The counter can be reset asynchronously via the reset signal (rst), which initializes the state to zero. The output consists of the current state of the flip-flops, providing a unique sequence that can be used for applications requiring a specific counting pattern.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input rst,
  output [n-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input rst,
  output [n-1:0] out
);parameter n = 4; // number of output signals (equal to the number of flip-flops in the circuit)

reg [n-1:0] state; // register to hold the current state

// define the sequence of binary states as a function of the flip-flops in the circuit
always @ (posedge clk or posedge rst) begin
  if (rst) begin
    state <= 0;
  end else begin
    state <= {state[n-2:0], ~state[n-1]};
  end
end

// connect the outputs of the flip-flops to the output signals of the module
assign out = state;

endmodule

