description:
Design a programmable logic array (PLA) that computes a specific Boolean output based on two input signals. The module generates two product terms: the logical AND and logical OR of the inputs (in1 and in2), and then applies an exclusive OR operation to these terms to produce the final output (out1). The circuit effectively demonstrates a combination of AND, OR, and XOR logic, enabling the realization of complex logical functions based on the input values.
module top_module(
  input in1,
  input in2,
  output out1
);

code:
module top_module(
  input in1,
  input in2,
  output out1
);// Define the product terms as Boolean functions of the input signals
  wire p1 = in1 & in2;
  wire p2 = in1 | in2;

  // Define the sum term as a Boolean function of the product terms
  wire s1 = p1 ^ p2;

  // Connect the inputs to the AND gates
  assign p1 = in1 & in2;
  assign p2 = in1 | in2;

  // Connect the AND gates to the OR gate
  assign out1 = s1;

endmodule

